      "benefit": "CI",
      "years": [2015, 2024],
      "pattern": "volatility",
      "direction": "dispersion",
      "magnitude": "A/E oscillates between ~0.76 and ~1.16; empirical SD ~0.15 vs Poisson 1/sqrt(E) ~0.03-0.06",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "evidence": [
        "ae_ci_by_year.csv: A/E = 0.768 (2015), 0.897 (2016), 1.136 (2017), 1.045 (2018), 0.756 (2019), 1.119 (2020), 0.972 (2021), 0.952 (2022), 1.163 (2023), 1.127 (2024)",
        "summary.json: CI overall_ae = 1.0193, indicating near-baseline level but with wide year-to-year swings",
        "Empirical SD of CI yearly A/E is ~0.15, materially larger than the Poisson expectation of roughly 0.03-0.06 for expected claim counts of ~600-1,900"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate CI claims definition, coding, severity, diagnosis/age-gender mix, expected-rate basis and data integrity; use ae_ci_age_gender.csv/png to locate drivers. Treat CI as overdispersed and avoid single-year Poisson z-score flags. Revisit CI pricing/valuation volatility assumptions if the dispersion reflects genuine claim experience rather than data or expectation-basis issues."
    }
  ]
}

